{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightSelfDuality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightSelfDuality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Hom.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.higgs_complex_volume_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.higgs_complex_volume_real","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L70-L77","doc":"**Keystone corollary.** For the self-dual Higgs knot, the complex volume is\npurely real: its bar-odd (CS / Q_β / Im) face is 0 and its bar-even\n(Vol / mass / Re) face is `2V`. Hence `Q_β` cannot be the figure-eight's own\nimaginary face — it must live in the many-body binding defect (see the\nCAL-123 reanalysis audit). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:self-dual-higgs-real-volume","label":"prop:self-dual-higgs-real-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/self-dual-higgs-real-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.recurrence_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.recurrence_descent","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L56-L68","doc":"**Recurrence descent (the c_k ladder).** A three-term recurrence\n`Vp = c·Vk − Vm` with a σ-fixed (bar-even) multiplier `c` descends to BOTH\nparity recurrences at once — the algebraic engine of the c_k ladder\n(bar-even binding `c₂=−8` and bar-odd Q_β `c₂=−1` from one relation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.selfDual_barEven_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.selfDual_barEven_two","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L51-L54","doc":"For a self-dual element only the bar-EVEN (Vol / mass) face survives:\n`barEven σ V = 2V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.selfDual_barOdd_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.selfDual_barOdd_zero","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L45-L49","doc":"**Self-duality kills the imaginary face.** A σ-fixed (amphichiral /\nself-dual) element — the figure-eight 4_1 / Higgs — has zero bar-ODD part.\nThis is CS(4_1) = 0 = Im V(4_1), proved over any `(R, σ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.barEven_add_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.barEven_add_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The two parities reconstruct `2V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.barOdd","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L38-L39","doc":"bar-ODD part: `V − σV` (sinh / Chern–Simons / Q_β / Im face). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.barEven","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightSelfDuality.lean#L35-L36","doc":"bar-EVEN part: `V + σV` (cosh / Vol / binding / Re face). ","signatureChunk":0}]}